{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":13253,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"56e86cf4-de5b-5ba1-a173-95858530bc7f","total_cost_usd":0.219609,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8339,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"output_tokens":934,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8339,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":934,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8339},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5104,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005204,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":934,"cacheReadInputTokens":905,"cacheCreationInputTokens":8339,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21440499999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":true,\"reasons\":[\"The declared independent-unit column colony_id is consistent with the frozen data: exactly 12 colony codes (LG-01..LG-06, FR-01..FR-06) each appear on exactly 4 rows, and colony-level attributes (reef_zone, depth_m) are constant within each colony_id, in both procedure arms (6 colonies per zone, 4 nubbins each).\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states that 'Every nubbin record in data/input.csv contributed one observation to the test' and reports n = 24 per zone with Welch df = 45.7, so the row-independent two-sample t-test (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) treated the 4 nubbins per colony as independent observations rather than aggregating to the 12 independent colonies (which would give n = 6 per arm and roughly df <= 10).\",\"The data description itself notes nubbins from the same colony share genotype, light/flow history and handling batch, confirming within-colony dependence that the reported procedure ignores; the effective sample size is 12 colonies, not 48 nubbins, so the reported p < 0.01 rests on pseudoreplication.\",\"The minted lock's unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly ['colony_id'], matching the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: colony_id' extracted in the translation receipt (token colony_id, present in the parsed logical header), with matching v1 lock digest sha256:00ca9e95...\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declared independent-unit column colony_id is consistent with the frozen data: exactly 12 colony codes (LG-01..LG-06, FR-01..FR-06) each appear on exactly 4 rows, and colony-level attributes (reef_zone, depth_m) are constant within each colony_id, in both procedure arms (6 colonies per zone, 4 nubbins each).","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states that 'Every nubbin record in data/input.csv contributed one observation to the test' and reports n = 24 per zone with Welch df = 45.7, so the row-independent two-sample t-test (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) treated the 4 nubbins per colony as independent observations rather than aggregating to the 12 independent colonies (which would give n = 6 per arm and roughly df <= 10).","The data description itself notes nubbins from the same colony share genotype, light/flow history and handling batch, confirming within-colony dependence that the reported procedure ignores; the effective sample size is 12 colonies, not 48 nubbins, so the reported p < 0.01 rests on pseudoreplication.","The minted lock's unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone: authorized_key_columns is exactly ['colony_id'], matching the quoted declaration 'Independent unit column: colony_id' extracted in the translation receipt (token colony_id, present in the parsed logical header), with matching v1 lock digest sha256:00ca9e95..."]},"ttft_ms":5348,"ttft_stream_ms":1522,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":11610,"uuid":"df0a63a1-0b47-4a28-a375-08b066989303"}
